Ohle Claussen wrote:
> On 2007-04-08, Janis Papanagnou wrote:
>>Tudor wrote:
>>
>>>I've just started playing nethack recently, and was wondering how I
>>>could tame more pets, and how to polymorph into different things.
>>
>>Taming:
>>Throw tripe to dogs and cats, throw herbs to horses.
> 
> Don't use tripe for taiming if you have other meaty food to spare. Tripe
> can be more useful to keep the pets near you and to train them for
> stealing. Even fortune cookies and meaty corpses can be used to tame cats
> and dogs.

I (partly) agree with that advice only because of the restriction "if you
have other meaty food to spare". In the beginning you may want to keep the
"people food" for yourself to prevent starvation (depending on the class
played). Training pets to rob shops is at most a secondary goal, primary
goal is to survive long enough. Monster meat needs to be fresh to tame a
dog; after 50 turns the monster will not get tame (which was the question)
any more if you throw that old food to him, and often you need the monster
meat yourself to stay alive. If you play a character that has no problems
with his food supply you can of course throw even food rations or, as you
suggested, a fortune cookie; because of it's low nutrition value you won't
lose a lot. But generally tripe rations is the prefered food for cats and
dogs because the player can't eat it (without drawbacks).

